---
export const prerender = true;
import BaseLayout from '../components/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About | Access Free Tools"
  description="Learn about Access Free Tools, a library of free calculators and everyday browser utilities."
  path="/about/"
>
  <section class="page-intro">
    <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / About</p>
    <h1>About Access Free Tools</h1>
    <p>
      Access Free Tools is a practical library of calculators, converters, text tools, browser AI
      helpers, and everyday utilities. The focus is speed, clear explanations, privacy-aware tool
      behavior, and pages that are easy to use on desktop or mobile.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section content-section-narrow">
    <h2>How tools are made</h2>
    <p>
      Each utility uses clear controls, helpful examples, and plain-language instructions so the
      page stays useful before anything else.
    </p>
    <div class="feature-list">
      <p><strong>Plain language:</strong> formulas, inputs, and results should be understandable without hunting through a long article first.</p>
      <p><strong>Useful guides:</strong> blog posts are tied to the actual Access Free Tools calculator or utility.</p>
      <p><strong>Privacy-aware tools:</strong> calculators are browser-first where practical, and AI pages explain model loading and upload limits.</p>
      <p><strong>Honest limits:</strong> finance, health, construction, electrical, AI, and other higher-trust pages explain when results are estimates.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section content-section-narrow">
    <h2>How the site stands out</h2>
    <p>
      Many calculator directories are useful because they are large. Access Free Tools is growing
      toward that same breadth while keeping a sharper promise: make each result easier to trust,
      explain, and double-check.
    </p>
    <p>
      The site is audited for metadata, sitemap coverage, broken links, structured data,
      performance budgets, lazy AI assets, and security checks before major GitHub updates.
    </p>
    <p>
      Read the public approach page for the practical standards used while new tools are added.
    </p>
    <p><a class="card-link" href="/why-access-free-tools/">Why Access Free Tools</a></p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
